Source-landscape note: The 2023 Mexico documentary universe is broad and multilingual, spanning UN/OHCHR mechanisms, IACHR/OAS records, Mexican government and CNDH documents, GIEI/Ayotzinapa investigations, Amnesty, HRW, Freedom House, ACLED, academic research, and reputable reporting. Major source families include militarized public security, arbitrary detention, enforced disappearance, Ayotzinapa, migrant detention, protest policing, gender violence, oversight, and official security outcomes. Search results were treated as leads only; no evidence claims or scores were extracted.

